{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, sorry your computer is giving you trouble again. I'd like to help, but I don't have a record of what \"the thing\" is, so I need a few details first:\n\n1. What exactly happens? For example: it's slow or freezes, it crashes or shows a blue screen, it won't turn on, it won't connect to Wi-Fi or VPN, or you see an error message. If there's an error, please send the exact wording or a photo of the screen.\n2. When does it happen? At startup, when you open a certain app, or at random?\n3. When did you last fully restart the laptop (Start > Power > Restart, not just closing the lid)?\n4. Did it start after an update or after installing something new?\n5. Are you still using your usual laptop (BL-LT-0107)? It hasn't connected to our management system for about 12 days. Has it been switched off, away from the office, or off the network?\n\nIf you haven't restarted it recently, please try a full restart in the meantime. That fixes a lot of recurring problems. Once I hear back, I'll get this sorted or pass it to the right team.",
  "internal_note": "Vague ticket: 'my computer is doing the thing again'. No prior ticket history available to identify the recurring issue. lookup_user: Sofia Rossi (user 7), Marketing, account active, 0 failed logins, not VIP, single device BL-LT-0107. check_device_status BL-LT-0107: Win11 Pro, OFFLINE, last check-in 2026-09-29 (warning: no check-in for 12 days), disk 54.7% free (140/256 GB), so low disk space is ruled out. The 12-day gap in check-ins could mean the device is off, off-network, or the agent is broken, and it may be connected to the issue. Asked the user for symptoms, error text, timing, last restart, recent changes, and whether she is still using this device. Suggested a full restart per KB-019 in case the issue is slowness or freezing. Next step: match her reply to the right KB article, or escalate if it's a crash or hardware fault, or if the device agent stays offline.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-019"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
